# Build context for the seven Java service images: the repository root.
# (docker-compose.yaml and Jenkinsfile.app-cicd both use `context: .`.)
#
# Docker reads only the .dockerignore at the root of the build context, so the
# per-service .dockerignore files that used to live in app/backend/*-svc/ were never
# applied and have been removed. The frontend and gateway use their own contexts
# (app/frontend, app/gateway); see app/frontend/.dockerignore.
#
# Allow-list: exclude everything, then re-include only what the Java Dockerfiles COPY
#   COPY pom.xml
#   COPY app/backend/<module>/pom.xml
#   COPY app/backend/<module>/src
# A new top-level file or directory therefore never leaks into an image build and never
# invalidates the Maven layer cache. The Dockerfile itself is always sent to the daemon.
*

!pom.xml
!app/backend/*/pom.xml
!app/backend/*/src

# Keep build output and local files out even if they appear under an allowed path.
**/target
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/.DS_Store
